      "headline": "OpenAI says a GPT-6.2 billing mistake means Astra users now reach usage limits 40% faster",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Let's start with a correction OpenAI made to its own bill. Alex, what happened?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "OpenAI's Thibault Sottiaux posted on X on November 26th that the company made a billing mistake at the launch of GPT-6.2, and had been incorrectly discounting usage of the Astra and Sol models for most users." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "And now that it's fixed?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "In OpenAI's own words, comparing to last week, you will reach your limits 40% faster on GPT-6.2 Astra and 25% faster on Sol. Other models weren't affected, OpenAI says it won't charge anyone for past usage, and it's adding one banked reset for people on Go, Plus, Pro and Business." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Two caveats worth saying out loud. These are the company's own numbers and they have not been independently verified, and TechRadar is a single source here. TechRadar also makes a fair point of arithmetic, that hitting a limit 40% faster is not the same thing as cutting the limit by 40%." }
